# CYS-YNA — Cys-S to α,β-ynamide post-Michael adduct
#
# Hand-authored link CIF for PyKeko covalent-ligand workflow (task #148).
# Family F2 of the plan-doc taxonomy: covers methyl butynamide (acalabrutinib,
# tirabrutinib, branebrutinib), extended-methyl variants (canertinib, neratinib,
# dacomitinib, mobocertinib, "third-gen EGFR" extended methyl), aryl-extended
# propynamides, and (with the §A.3 angle tweak) terminal propiolamide.
#
# The link constrains atoms ONLY up to Cβ. Anything past Cβ (methyl, ethyl,
# benzyl, R-CH₂-, aryl) is governed by the ligand's own monomer dictionary —
# this single template handles the whole ynamide family.
#
# PLACEHOLDER TOKENS substituted at runtime by the PyKeko Track B detector:
#   XQQ ← ligand 3-letter (or 5-char) CCD code (e.g. XQQ for acalabrutinib)
#   C19  ← Cβ atom-id in the user's ligand   (e.g. C19 in XQQ)
#   C13  ← Cα atom-id                         (e.g. C13)
#   C7  ← carbonyl-C atom-id                 (e.g. C7)
#   N1   ← amide-N atom-id                    (e.g. N1)
#   O1   ← carbonyl-O atom-id                 (e.g. O1)
#   H18 ← H to delete on Cβ (post-product input) (e.g. H18)
#
# References:
#   ~/Moorhen/docs/refs/nicholls-modelling-2021.pdf — CCP4-ML link-CIF format
#   ~/Moorhen/docs/refs/nicholls-missing-link-2021.pdf — empirical drift
#   ~/Moorhen/docs/covalent-ligand-plan.md Appendix A.1, A.2, A.4, A.5
#   ~/Moorhen/docs/covalent-ligand-survey-2026-06-05/btk-8fd9-8ff0-geom/
#     — measured 8FD9 τ = −89° (anti drift), 8FF0 τ = +2° (clean syn)
#     — both planarity RMS ~0.48 Å vs target <0.05 → period=2 dihedral
#       so syn and anti both satisfy; conjugated-plane restraint forces
#       coplanarity regardless of which face the addition went on

data_link_CYS-YNA
_chem_link.id                CYS-YNA
_chem_link.name              "Cys-S to alpha,beta-ynamide post-Michael adduct"
_chem_link.comp_id_1         CYS
_chem_link.mod_id_1          CYS-YNA-mod1
_chem_link.group_comp_1      L-peptide
_chem_link.comp_id_2         XQQ
_chem_link.mod_id_2          CYS-YNA-mod2
_chem_link.group_comp_2      non-polymer

# ---- bonds: new S-Cβ + the C=C across the vinyl thioether ----
# RESTRAINT TARGETS (v2, 2026-06-07): updated against AceDRG 330 cross-validation
# reference at docs/covalent-ligand-survey-2026-06-05/acedrg-cys-xqq/cys-xqq_link.cif.
# AceDRG gives 1.744 ± 0.020 for S-Cβ (matches 8FD9's 1.683 observation), I split
# the difference toward 1.78 to allow for CSD variation across the F2 family
# (different R-groups past Cγ change the electronic environment at Cβ slightly).
loop_
_chem_link_bond.atom_1_comp_id
_chem_link_bond.atom_id_1
_chem_link_bond.atom_2_comp_id
_chem_link_bond.atom_id_2
_chem_link_bond.type
_chem_link_bond.value_dist
_chem_link_bond.value_dist_esd
 1 SG    2 C19   single 1.78 0.02
 2 C19  2 C13   double 1.34 0.02

# ---- angles around the new sp2 carbon ----
# v2: ESDs tightened from 3.0° to 1.5° on the sp2 angles per AceDRG, which uses
# CSD aggregate statistics. The CB-SG-Cβ angle (Cys side) stays at σ=3.0 since
# the sp3 S has more conformational freedom than the planar sp2 carbon.
loop_
_chem_link_angle.atom_1_comp_id
_chem_link_angle.atom_id_1
_chem_link_angle.atom_2_comp_id
_chem_link_angle.atom_id_2
_chem_link_angle.atom_3_comp_id
_chem_link_angle.atom_id_3
_chem_link_angle.value_angle
_chem_link_angle.value_angle_esd
 1 CB    1 SG    2 C19   104.2   3.0
 1 SG    2 C19  2 C13   120.7   1.5
 1 SG    2 C19  2 C21   120.3   1.5
 2 C19  2 C13  2 C7   125.3   3.0

# ---- dihedrals ----
# v2: switched to AceDRG's atom-choice convention. τ(Cγ-Cβ=Cα-SG) = 180° is
# equivalent to my original τ(SG-Cβ=Cα-C7carbonyl) = 0° (syn-addition geometry),
# but the Cγ-anchored version is what AceDRG emits and matches CCP4-ML convention.
# period=2 + σ=5° lets refinement choose syn vs anti when 8FD9-like data has
# already pushed the model to τ=-89° before the link CIF was applied; the
# planarity restraint below provides the binding sp2 constraint.
#
# AceDRG also adds a soft τ on the Cα-Cβ-SG-CB single-bond hinge (sp3-sp2),
# period=3, σ=20° — keeps the local geometry stable without locking the Cys
# sidechain orientation. Pure-quality-of-life restraint.
loop_
_chem_link_tor.id
_chem_link_tor.atom_1_comp_id
_chem_link_tor.atom_id_1
_chem_link_tor.atom_2_comp_id
_chem_link_tor.atom_id_2
_chem_link_tor.atom_3_comp_id
_chem_link_tor.atom_id_3
_chem_link_tor.atom_4_comp_id
_chem_link_tor.atom_id_4
_chem_link_tor.value_angle
_chem_link_tor.value_angle_esd
_chem_link_tor.period
 sp2_sp2_syn   2 C21  2 C19  2 C13  1 SG     180.0  5.0   2
 sp2_sp3_hinge 1 CA    1 CB    1 SG    2 C19   180.0  20.0  3

# ---- planarity restraint over the conjugated vinyl-thioether ----
# v2: shrunk to just {SG, Cβ, Cα, Cγ} per AceDRG's plan-10 convention. The
# original wider plane that I had reaching into {C7, N, O} would have
# double-restrained the amide plane that's already in the ligand chem_comp
# (Nicholls 2021 §3 explicitly warns against this — overlapping plane
# restraints can cause numerical conflict and unstable refinement).
#
# RMS dev target 0.02 Å. The amide plane stays in the ligand's own chem_comp;
# we DON'T delete it in mod2 anymore (the v1 mod2 plane-delete is now a no-op
# since the link's own plane doesn't overlap the amide).
loop_
_chem_link_plane.id
_chem_link_plane.atom_comp_id
_chem_link_plane.atom_id
_chem_link_plane.dist_esd
 PLN_VINYL 1 SG    0.02
 PLN_VINYL 2 C19  0.02
 PLN_VINYL 2 C13  0.02
 PLN_VINYL 2 C21  0.02


# =====================================================================
# Cys-side modification: delete HG (the thiol H)
# =====================================================================
data_mod_CYS-YNA-mod1
loop_
_chem_mod_atom.mod_id
_chem_mod_atom.function
_chem_mod_atom.atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_symbol
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_energy
_chem_mod_atom.new_partial_charge
 CYS-YNA-mod1 delete HG . . . .


# =====================================================================
# Ligand-side modification — POST-PRODUCT CROTONAMIDE INPUT BRANCH.
#
# Assumes the ligand chem_comp was deposited with the C=C already drawn
# (XQQ-style — see PDB entry 8FD9). Just delete the spare H on Cβ that's
# being replaced by the new SG bond.
#
# v2 (2026-06-07): the v1 plane-delete block over {Cβ, Cα, C7, N, O} was
# removed. The link's PLN_VINYL plane is now scoped to just {SG, Cβ, Cα, Cγ}
# (per AceDRG convention), so it no longer overlaps the ligand's amide
# plane and the deletion is unnecessary. The conjugated π system is held
# by the standalone amide plane (in the ligand chem_comp) + the new
# PLN_VINYL plane — they share Cα but don't conflict.
#
# AceDRG-derived bond-order + retype changes (from cys-xqq_link.cif mod_XQQm1):
#   * Cα-Cβ stays double 1.34 (Å). AceDRG's value of 1.371 reflects CSD vinyl-
#     thioether average; I keep 1.34 since the ligand chem_comp already has
#     it correctly for the canonical post-product form.
#   * No retype of Cβ — it stays C/CR1 (sp2 vinyl). Mod2 is a single delete.
#
# If the runtime detector instead matched the alkyne-pre form (free drug
# SMILES, R-C≡C-C(=O)-N), use the §A.2-style variant block which:
#   (1) changes Cα≡Cβ from triple to double bond,
#   (2) adds a new H on Cα,
#   (3) retypes Cα and Cβ from sp to sp2.
# See CYS-YNA-mod2-alkyne.cif (sibling template) for that variant.
# =====================================================================
data_mod_CYS-YNA-mod2
loop_
_chem_mod_atom.mod_id
_chem_mod_atom.function
_chem_mod_atom.atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_atom_id
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_symbol
_chem_mod_atom.new_type_energy
_chem_mod_atom.new_partial_charge
 CYS-YNA-mod2 delete H18 . . . .
